# //// Neoffice — commit-the-build. Upstream ignores its vite output (mint/public/mint
# //// and mint/www/mint.html) and rebuilds on every install; our client VMs have 2 GB of
# //// RAM and vite dies there, so the built SPA is committed and instances only pull it.
# //// The two upstream lines are kept commented out, not deleted, so the next merge sees
# //// exactly what upstream ignored. Drop this and restore them the day instances build.
# 2026-05-07 (NORA #28) — frontend build outputs are committed on this branch.
# See docs/COMMIT-BUILD-PATTERN.md in neoffice-devops.
# (Mint writes vite output to public/mint/ instead of public/frontend/, see
# vite.config.ts --base=/assets/mint/mint/.)
# mint/public/mint
mint/public/node_modules
# //// Neoffice — same commit-the-build reason: mint/www/mint.html is the Jinja entry
# //// copied out of the vite build (yarn copy-html-entry) and is committed with it.
# //// CLAUDE.md is unshipped on purpose (690eed9) — it documents that pipeline.
# mint/www/mint.html
# CLAUDE.md  # 2026-05-07 unshipped to document commit-the-build pipeline
